1
00:00:03,435 --> 00:00:05,675
(Penny:)Leonard, what time does
your mom's plane get in?

2
00:00:05,673 --> 00:00:07,043
(Leonard:)I don't know--
some time tomorrow morning.

3
00:00:07,041 --> 00:00:08,941
(Penny:)Don't you want
to know for sure?

4
00:00:08,943 --> 00:00:11,643
(Leonard:)No need to. As soon as she flies
into California airspace,

5
00:00:11,645 --> 00:00:13,515
(Leonard:)I'll feel a disturbance
in the Force.

6
00:00:15,281 --> 00:00:17,281
(Amy:)It's so nice
both of your moms are coming in

7
00:00:17,284 --> 00:00:18,954
(Amy:)to see you guys get an award.

8
00:00:18,953 --> 00:00:22,123
(Sheldon:)Well, my mother's been there
for every honor I've won

9
00:00:22,123 --> 00:00:23,953
(Sheldon:)since I beat out my twin sister

10
00:00:23,958 --> 00:00:25,558
for the "did it
on the potty" trophy.

11
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,690
(Sheldon:)How does this look?

12
00:00:28,696 --> 00:00:31,026
(Penny:)Aw, it's so nice.
She's gonna love it.

13
00:00:31,032 --> 00:00:32,362
(Amy:)Sure, his mom gets roses.

14
00:00:32,366 --> 00:00:33,666
(Amy:)When I want them,

15
00:00:33,667 --> 00:00:36,367
they're a "bouquet of
severed plant genitals."

16
00:00:37,570 --> 00:00:38,900
(Sheldon:)You act like I didn't get you

17
00:00:38,906 --> 00:00:41,236
(Sheldon:)that mushroom log
on Valentine's Day.

18
00:00:41,242 --> 00:00:42,812
(Amy:)He's right.

19
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:46,250
(Amy:)Roses die, but a moist rotting
log will pump out mushrooms

20
00:00:46,247 --> 00:00:48,917
(Amy:)for two or three magical years.

21
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:50,916
(Penny:)You know,
your mom's never been

22
00:00:50,918 --> 00:00:50,918
(Penny:)too thrilled
with our relationship.

23
00:00:50,918 --> 00:00:54,058
(Penny:)Maybe I should get her something
so she warms up to me.

24
00:00:54,055 --> 00:00:55,725
(Leonard:)If you could run
out and get a PhD,

25
00:00:55,723 --> 00:00:58,093
(Leonard:)that might make
her like you.

26
00:00:58,092 --> 00:01:01,532
(Penny:)Really?
It didn't work for you.

27
00:01:01,529 --> 00:01:03,029
(Amy:)Do you think
the moms will get along?

28
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:04,830
(Leonard:)Uh, I don't know.
They're pretty different.

29
00:01:04,832 --> 00:01:06,702
(Sheldon:)Maybe they'll be best friends.

30
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:09,700
(Sheldon:)One of them is brilliant,
one is sweet and simple.

31
00:01:09,703 --> 00:01:12,573
(Sheldon:)Sound familiar?

32
00:01:12,573 --> 00:01:16,073
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

